  "raw_meta_yaml": "# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prefix-dev/recipe-format/main/schema.json\nschema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.7.0\"\n\npackage:\n  # Upstream npm `name` is `caveman-installer`; both `caveman` slots (PyPI + npm)\n  # are taken by unrelated dormant projects, so we keep the upstream name here.\n  # The installed CLI is `caveman-install` (per package.json `bin` map).\n  name: caveman-installer\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 0f8b833ef65be67b565573d075264b7acab645e80241cfdae016421211d41147\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - set -ex\n        - NPM_VER=$(node -p \"require('./package.json').version\")\n        - pnpm install --prod --ignore-scripts\n        - pnpm-licenses generate-disclaimer --prod --output-file=ThirdPartyLicenses.txt\n        - npm pack --ignore-scripts --userconfig nonexistentrc\n        - npm install --userconfig nonexistentrc --global \"${SRC_DIR}/caveman-installer-${NPM_VER}.tgz\"\n        - find \"${PREFIX}/lib/node_modules/caveman-installer\" -type d -name .bin -exec rm -rf {} + || true\n      else:\n        - for /f \"delims=\" %%v in ('node -p \"require('./package.json').version\"') do set NPM_VER=%%v\n        - call pnpm install --prod --ignore-scripts\n        - if %ERRORLEVEL% neq 0 exit 1\n        - call pnpm-licenses generate-disclaimer --prod --output-file=ThirdPartyLicenses.txt\n        - if %ERRORLEVEL% neq 0 exit 1\n        - call npm pack --ignore-scripts --userconfig nonexistentrc\n        - if %ERRORLEVEL% neq 0 exit 1\n        - call npm install --userconfig nonexistentrc --global \"%SRC_DIR%/caveman-installer-%NPM_VER%.tgz\"\n        - if %ERRORLEVEL% neq 0 exit 1\n        - for /d /r \"%PREFIX%\\node_modules\\caveman-installer\" %%d in (.bin) do if exist \"%%d\" rd /s /q \"%%d\"\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - nodejs >=18\n    - pnpm\n    - pnpm-licenses\n  host:\n    - nodejs 24.*\n  run:\n    - nodejs >=18\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - caveman-install --help\n\nabout:\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - LICENSE.BSL\n    - LICENSING.md\n    - ThirdPartyLicenses.txt\n  summary: One-shot installer that wires the caveman Claude Code skill into ~30 AI coding agents\n  description: |\n    caveman is a Claude Code skill that cuts ~65% of tokens by talking like\n    caveman. This package installs the `caveman` CLI, a one-shot bootstrapper\n    that auto-detects supported AI coding agents on the machine (Claude Code,\n    Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, opencode, Continue, Cline, Windsurf, and\n    ~25 more) and runs each agent's native install path. It also wires\n    Claude Code hooks, a statusline badge, and the `caveman-shrink` MCP\n    middleware when those targets are present. Idempotent and re-runnable.\n  homepage: https://getcaveman.dev/\n  repository: https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman\n  documentation: https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman/blob/main/INSTALL.md\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - rxm7706\n",
